#  PGDSpider
# To run ADMIXTURE or BayesAss, we need to provide an input file. The program PGDSpider is able to convert .vcf files to (amongst others) .geno format, which ADMIXTURE can read, or Immanc format (.inp), which BayesAss can read. This requires 4 files:

#1) The input data file in .vcf format (generated with MAF filter)

#2) A text file with sample IDs and the population designations. For instance:
#Ind1       Pop3
#Ind2       Pop1
#Ind3       Pop2

#3) A settings file (.spid) that tells PGDSpider how to process the data:
# This can be retrieved from PGDSpider2 GUI. Fill in all the questions and then press ‘Create/Edit SPID file')
# You can download PGDspider here: PGDSpider version 2.1.1.5 (unibe.ch)

#4) A bash script that runs the program with all the above settings specified (dont forget to load the Java module):
java -Xmx1024m -Xms512m -jar /services/tools/pgdspider/2.1.1.5 -inputfile /folder/VCF/Chromrenam.vcf -inputformat VCF -outputfile /folder/PGD/Output.inp -outpuformat IMMANC -spid /folder/PGD/Info.spid

# STARTUP
BA3-SNPS -i 10000000 -b 1000000 -n 1000 -s 1000 -v -g -t -m0.07 -a0.20 -f0.40 -l 7 -F Output.inp -o Bayes1.txt
